+# Complete backend deployment, 2026-10-17
+
+The owner explicitly requests the full latest backend after the installed game reports an incompatible server contract. FB01 deploys the complete current Python backend and Studio; FB02 includes the actual matching compiler27 / physics0.66 / rules22 native verifier; FB03 appends matching immutable published track revisions while retaining original documents, old versions, scores and player data; FB04 applies the same tested image to the cloud and existing PC service. This supersedes the earlier deployment's deliberate physics0.59/rules20 pin.
+
+The previous phone APK uses physics0.64/rules22. Updating the backend to latest0.66 does not make that old APK compatible. A matching game update remains necessary; this task does not inspect a phone connection, build/install an APK or perform physical-phone testing.
+
+Sources are frozen before building. The complete Python source tree replaces the old tree, including removal of the retired legacy authoring module, so old files cannot remain accidentally importable. Dependencies retain their exact existing lock. The additive maintenance write gate is retained in the frozen package. The no-prop oval golden advances its expected physics field from0.65 to0.66; the actual native build must still reproduce the same document, inputs, five-lap timing and rewind result. No racing check is bypassed and no older simulation is relabelled as the latest one.
+
+Cloud API, worker and every existing job receive one tested digest. A fresh managed SQL backup precedes the write fence. Original semantic rows, the ordinary600-player Studio history and achievement state are fingerprinted while writers are paused. New revisions are appended for every visible published head, including community tracks. Old versions/documents, records and competitions remain stored; their pinned historical contracts are not rewritten. Existing external-provider, notification and continuous-monitoring settings remain in force.
+
+Weekly Rivalry membership and matchmaking include the actual build contract key, so the latest build enters a compatible field using matching published revisions. Challenge discovery filters by the active contract; incompatible historical challenges remain stored and retain their results. Their original timing evidence is not reused as a new-physics result.
+
+The existing PC project receives the same image and a frozen source bind. Its original credentials, PostgreSQL volume and object volume remain. API/worker writers pause for a complete logical SQL dump and immutable-object archive; original semantic rows are compared across migration and catalog revision insertion. The previously unhealthy PC API health probe is aligned with the existing `/ready` route.
+
+Actual commands, initial failures and final outcomes belong in `docs/evidence/full-backend-deploy-2026-10-17/`. The first complete test collection exposed missing repository mounts/imports in the isolated harness; the corrected harness mounts the entire frozen test root. This was a test setup failure before assertions ran. Deployment completion and test counts must be taken from the final receipt and logs, not this prepared procedure.
+
+The initial broad audit was stopped after800 passes,25 failures,56 skips and two setup errors in1217.54s; it is not a complete-suite pass. It exposed the owner-hide/share-link regression and a stale exported checkpoint-transition constant, both corrected in runtime source. The share-link regression check and existing Studio quarantine check pass together. Historical upload expectations are updated to the retired endpoint's410 response while the active publication endpoint retains its explicit terms gate. The two-player integration now records an actual creator-start lap, publishes its verified trajectory, records real five-lap races and waits for bounded idle projections before checking histogram totals. It retains idempotent upload, rating, tied ranking, exact recording and invalid-score assertions.
+
+Other initial failures were test fixtures: changing an explicit historical authoring fixture into development mode without restoring the current draft policy; assuming histogram/backfill was the worker's next idle job before achievement projection; omitting explicit community acceptance in the multi-process publication helper; and missing load-test golden/country-art inputs in the isolated image test environment. PowerShell-native transport/privacy tests now run on Windows rather than attempting to launch PowerShell inside Linux. The saved-recovery size fixture receives its required tick_rate so it reaches the existing terminal413 path instead of failing its contract before HTTP. No runtime client retry policy is changed.
+
+The final candidate again passes the actual Linux oval replay/rewind checks. All28 public document byte hashes and their new native manifests are verified read-only against that exact image before catalog mutation. Windows transport/privacy checks pass (two tests), and saved native wire/charge-recovery checks pass (five tests); their initial failed size-fixture attempt is retained. The extended follow-up was also stopped during artificial-driver calibration (203 passes, two fixture failures,15 skips). The final gate focuses on deployment-relevant race, publication, achievement, economy, Studio, privacy, migration and worker behavior; it does not claim a complete calibration or full-suite pass. Initial and final passes are reported separately.
+
+Operational entry points:
+
+```powershell
+.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/full_backend_deploy_20261017.py <stage>
+.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/full_backend_pc_20261017.py <stage>
+```
+
+The staged rollout follows inspect/extract/freeze/prepare/build/test/push/backup/preview, then maintenance/snapshot/migrate/catalog/canary/promote/smoke/catalog-http/browser/finish. The PC rollout follows prepare/backup/snapshot/migrate/preview/catalog/promote/verify. Mutating stages that share a receipt run sequentially.
+
+## Completed rollout
+
+Cloud API **bmt-stg-e7a444ab-api-00081-lat**, one matching worker and **all five owned job definitions** now use `europe-west1-docker.pkg.dev/beat-my-track/bmt-stg-e7a444ab-images/backend@sha256:8707116d7acaf1a8ced96d231402eccc3a461742ccb1274bcc1260b923f55c4c`. The same image serves the existing PC API/worker. Both advertise compiler27 / physics0.66 / rules22 on pinned Godot4.7.2. Cloud schema remains42; PC advances35 to42. Cloud write maintenance is restored and temporary tags/lock are removed. Backup **1792262296541** is successful; the complete quiesced PC SQL dump/object archive and SHA256 receipts remain private under the owned build directory.
+
+All56 selected cloud semantic table fingerprints are exact across migration and catalog insertion. All62 original PC table fingerprints are exact across35-to42 migration and catalog insertion when selecting the original revision population. PC retains15 original players,190 original runs and154 original versions;27 matching versions bring the catalog to181. The catalog trigger adds270 new histogram rows for those versions; all888 original histogram rows retain their exact complete row hash. The cloud appends28 matching versions. All28 new public heads/documents, all28 immediately previous links and two earlier official links per each of27 official tracks are checked live. The600-player Studio history, cases, incidents and financial/Coin ledgers remain.
+
+The focused gate initially reports390 passes, five fixture failures and nine skips in571.40s. Four POSIX cases pass after the process producer explicitly accepts current community terms. The full-client SDK check passes separately on Windows: its current script contains13 semantic checks, with no legacy upload call; backend-only images lack its presentation assets. The remaining Windows checks comprise two network/privacy tests and five saved-recovery tests. The final archive utility passes its archive/restore/corruption regression. No simulation, score, auth, quarantine or idempotency invariant is removed. The broad audits and their actual failures remain in the evidence directory; no full artificial-driver calibration, production load or managed restore pass is claimed.
+
+The inherited object archive utility was older than the current recipe. The final image adds exactly the current utility; **all API and canonical file hashes are byte-exact to the API test image6bf0fb5a**. Its utility test runs on the final image; the final cloud native/schema/storage smoke and HTTP checks also run on that image. Registry pulls verify the immutable image identity. Python remains the pinned3.12.15. Image IDs use the OCI index in this engine; registry identity is checked by pulling the digest rather than equating its child config digest with the index ID.
+
+Inventory inspection also finds the older manual `pace2` job omitted from prior deployment lists. Its default program/permissions remain and its definition receives the full image; its last failed historical execution is retained and it is not started. Other runtime settings, secrets and IAM remain. No new external monitoring/provider, notification or scheduler is activated.
+
+Live Studio passes58 read-only Edge checks at1440px and390px, with600 full-window /369 recent active players, no JavaScript errors, failed admin reads, write requests or global overflow. All19 assets match the release source. Cloud and PC report one matching healthy worker each. The final shared receipt reloads the successful browser child result before cleanup; the first cleanup assertion and its correction caused no traffic/data change.
+
+The first PC catalog adapter attempt named the storage protocol rather than its concrete local implementation and failed before catalog writes; the corrected adapter mounts objects read-only. An initial all-row cache comparison then correctly noticed the270 newly created cache rows. A separate read-only hash check proves all888 old rows exact before the preservation selector is restricted to original revision IDs. The idempotent repeat adds zero further versions. These attempts and their receipts are retained.
+
+The installed phone snapshot remains physics0.64. A matching game update is required before that older client can race against this latest backend. No phone connection check, physical-phone test, APK build or installation is performed by this task. Existing historical competition contracts are retained; their scores are not converted into new-physics scores. Owner workflow/feel, separate artificial-driver calibration and production load/restore acceptance remain.
